---
layout: base.njk
navActive: support
title: "Support Elixir"
description: "Elixir is free to use and independently run. What keeping it going costs, how to sponsor it on GitHub, how running a collector differs from sponsoring, and where the record stands."
permalink: /support/index.html
canonical: /support
---
{#-
  One argument on one page: the sponsor button first, then why the record
  matters, what the money pays for, GitHub Sponsors, the collector alternative
  and the counters.

  The whole page rests on one promise, at the top and at the foot: sponsorship
  changes nothing about an account. Supercell's Fan Content Policy forbids
  selling access, and reading is universal by design (docs/roles). Every number
  is baked from the same stats endpoint /data reads, so the page can never quote
  a figure the data page would contradict. The section ids are links people
  hold.
-#}
{%- set t = stats.totals %}
{%- set n = "unknown" %}
{%- set sponsorUrl = "https://github.com/sponsors/jthingelstad" %}
<div class="page-head">
  <div>
    <h1 class="hero-title">Support Elixir</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Elixir is free to use and independently run. Keeping it going takes
      storage, compute, APIs, AI services, and collection that never stops.
      If the record is useful to you, you can help pay for it.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="support-actions">
  <a class="btn btn--gold" href="{{ sponsorUrl }}" rel="noopener">{% icon "heart", 17 %}Sponsor Elixir on GitHub</a>
  <a class="btn" href="/docs/operators">{% icon "server", 17 %}Run a collector</a>
</div>
<p class="footnote support-note">
  Voluntary, and that is the whole arrangement: no extra quota, no longer
  retention, no features, no priority. Supercell&rsquo;s
  <a href="https://www.supercell.com/fan-content-policy">Fan Content Policy</a>
  forbids selling access, and we would not want to sell it anyway.
</p>

<section class="data-sec" id="why">
  <div class="data-sec__head">
    <h2>Clash Royale forgets. Elixir remembers.</h2>
    <a class="data-sec__link" href="/data#what-is-recorded">What is recorded ›</a>
  </div>
  <p class="footnote">
    The game&rsquo;s API answers now. It holds the last handful of battles, the
    current roster, a rolling window of war weeks, and everything older is gone,
    not archived. Elixir records history while it still exists, so the same
    question can be asked next season.
  </p>
  <section class="panel">
    <div class="data-rows data-rows--three" role="table" aria-label="What the game's API holds and what Elixir holds">
      <div class="data-rows__row data-rows__row--head" role="row"><span role="columnheader">What</span><span role="columnheader">The game&rsquo;s API</span><span role="columnheader">Elixir</span></div>
      <div class="data-rows__row" role="row"><b role="cell">Battles</b><span role="cell" data-col="The game&rsquo;s API">about the last 30 per player</span><span role="cell" data-col="Elixir">every battle recorded{% if t %} since {{ t.oldest_battle | shortDay }}{% endif %}</span></div>
      <div class="data-rows__row" role="row"><b role="cell">Player history</b><span role="cell" data-col="The game&rsquo;s API">current profile only</span><span role="cell" data-col="Elixir">a daily record{% if t %}, {{ t.snapshots | number }} so far{% endif %}</span></div>
      <div class="data-rows__row" role="row"><b role="cell">Trophy progression</b><span role="cell" data-col="The game&rsquo;s API">current and best</span><span role="cell" data-col="Elixir">every daily reading, day by day</span></div>
      <div class="data-rows__row" role="row"><b role="cell">Deck usage</b><span role="cell" data-col="The game&rsquo;s API">not exposed</span><span role="cell" data-col="Elixir">derived from recorded battles</span></div>
      <div class="data-rows__row" role="row"><b role="cell">Clan history</b><span role="cell" data-col="The game&rsquo;s API">current roster</span><span role="cell" data-col="Elixir">roster history, read often while members play</span></div>
      <div class="data-rows__row" role="row"><b role="cell">Clan wars</b><span role="cell" data-col="The game&rsquo;s API">rolling ten weeks</span><span role="cell" data-col="Elixir">{% if t %}{{ t.war_weeks | number }} war weeks and counting{% else %}every war week, past the API&rsquo;s window{% endif %}</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <p class="footnote">
    No sponsor owns any part of the record. Sponsorship pays to keep the archive
    running; what is in it belongs to the people and clans who asked us to
    record them.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="data-sec" id="costs">
  <div class="data-sec__head"><h2>What sponsorship pays for</h2></div>
  <p class="footnote">High level, and honestly mundane. This is the bill for keeping a record that grows every day.</p>
  <div class="stats support-costs">
    {%- set costs = [
      ["Storage and backups", "database", "The record grows every day, and so do the backups that keep it safe."],
      ["App and API infrastructure", "server", "The service that answers agents, this site, and the work waiting behind them."],
      ["Continuous collection", "radar", "Battle, player, clan and river-race reads that run every few minutes."],
      ["AI and model usage", "bot", "The AI agents that help maintain the service and answer feedback."],
      ["Monitoring and tooling", "activity", "Alarms, request budgets and the admin tools: how a gap gets noticed."],
      ["Long-term retention", "archive", "Keeping history past the point the game's API drops it. Keeps what it records while someone tracks it, and for a year after."]
    ] %}
    {%- for c in costs %}
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="support-costs__name">{% icon c[1], 15 %}{{ c[0] }}</div>
      <div class="support-costs__text">{{ c[2] }}</div>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{#- Suggested amounts, not tiers: the word "tier" already means something on
    this site (docs/roles), and these must never be confused with it. -#}
<section class="data-sec" id="sponsors">
  <div class="data-sec__head"><h2>GitHub Sponsors</h2></div>
  <section class="panel">
    <div class="data-rows data-rows--levels">
      {%- set levels = [
        ["Elixir Supporter", "$5 / month", "Help keep Elixir running and preserving Clash Royale history."],
        ["Elixir Steward", "$10 / month", "Cover a steady share of storage, collection and the daily running costs."],
        ["Elixir Sustainer", "$20 / month", "Additional support for the long-term operation and growth of Elixir."]
      ] %}
      {%- for l in levels %}
      <div class="data-rows__row"><b>{{ l[0] }}</b><span>{{ l[2] }}</span><span class="mono">{{ l[1] }}</span></div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
  <p class="support-actions support-actions--foot"><a class="btn btn--gold" href="{{ sponsorUrl }}" rel="noopener">{% icon "heart", 17 %}Sponsor Elixir on GitHub</a></p>
</section>

{#- The one place on this page where something DOES change an account (running
    a collector raises your limits to Family), so the separation from
    sponsorship is stated rather than left to inference. -#}
<section class="data-sec" id="collector">
  <div class="data-sec__head"><h2>Contribute capacity instead</h2></div>
  <p class="footnote">
    A collector is a small process you run that fetches Clash Royale data on
    Elixir&rsquo;s behalf and hands it to Elixir. More collectors means more of
    the game recorded, more often. Running one raises your limits to Family, and
    nothing else: capacity you contributed coming back to you, not a reward for
    paying.
  </p>
  <p class="support-actions support-actions--foot">
    <a class="btn" data-session-face="in" href="/settings/collectors">Raise your hand</a>
    <a class="btn" data-session-face="out" href="/docs/operators">Read how collectors work</a>
  </p>
</section>

<section class="data-sec" id="record">
  <div class="data-sec__head"><h2>Where the record stands</h2></div>
  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">Battles</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.battles | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">Players</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.players_recording | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">War weeks</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.war_weeks | number }}{% else %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="footnote">
    Same numbers as <a href="/data">Status and data</a>, from the same statistics
    endpoint, not a fundraising figure.{% if t %} Read by
    {{ t.collectors_active | number }} active
    collector{% if t.collectors_active != 1 %}s{% endif %}; the oldest recorded
    battle is from {{ t.oldest_battle | shortDay }}.{% else %} Figures arrive
    when the site is next published.{% endif %}
  </p>
</section>

<p class="footnote">
  Elixir is a free community project. Sponsorship is optional and gives no
  additional features, quota, retention, or access, at any amount. The record
  stays the same for everyone reading it.
</p>
